title: Kanas/migrating async std to tokio
doc:
- audience: Todo
  description: |-
    # Description

    This PR removes the deprecated `async-std` dependency from the `polkadot-sdk` workspace and replaces it with `tokio` within the `bridges/relays` crates.

    `async-std` has been deprecated as of March 2025. Since `tokio` is already heavily utilized as a workspace dependency, the affected crates were migrated to use `tokio` primitives (`Arc`, `Mutex`, `RwLock`, `sleep`, `spawn`, `block_on`) and `async-channel`.

    Affected crates:
    - `equivocation-detector`
    - `finality-relay`
    - `messages-relay`
    - `parachains-relay`
    - `relay-substrate-client`
    - `relay-utils`
    - `substrate-relay-helper`

    Closes https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/issues/10874

    ## Integration

    Reviewers and downstream projects should ensure that `tokio` is now the expected async runtime for any binaries running the bridges relay components. The integration should be seamless for existing deployments as the `polkadot-sdk` already sets up `tokio` runtimes for its nodes.

    ## Review Notes

    - Replaced `async_std::sync::{Arc, Mutex, RwLock}` with `std::sync::Arc` and `tokio::sync::{Mutex, RwLock}` directly.
    - Replaced `async_std::task::sleep` and `async_std::task::spawn` with `tokio::time::sleep` and `tokio::spawn` respectively.
    - For top-level nested blocking operations where `async_std::task::block_on` was used, `tokio::runtime::Runtime::new().unwrap().block_on(...)` has been implemented to establish an isolated runtime for those specific tasks (e.g., in `guard.rs` and `transaction_tracker.rs`).
    - Replaced `async_std::channel` with `async-channel` since `std::sync::mpsc` doesn't strictly cover all the same async receiver scenarios needed by the caching/subscription clients.
    - Converted `#[async_std::test]` to `#[tokio::test]`.
    - Updated `tokio::task_local!` to `std::thread_local!` inside `initialize.rs` to match the exact `LOOP_NAME` string manipulation originally modeled by `async_std::task_local!`.

    ### Validation
    - Compilation: Verified that the workspace compiles successfully without async-std across all updated crates using cargo check and dealing with residual compilation issues like missing dependencies and types.
    - Unit Tests: All 125 unit tests across the 7 crates passed seamlessly, confirming that our tokio primitives are correctly dropping into the spots left by async-std.
    ```bash
    cargo check -p equivocation-detector -p finality-relay -p messages-relay -p parachains-relay -p relay-substrate-client -p relay-utils -p substrate-relay-helper
    cargo test -p equivocation-detector -p finality-relay -p messages-relay -p parachains-relay -p relay-substrate-client -p relay-utils -p substrate-relay-helper
    ```

    # Checklist

    * [x] My PR includes a detailed description as outlined in the "Description" and its two subsections above.
    * [x] My PR follows the [labeling requirements](https://github.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/blob/master/docs/contributor/CONTRIBUTING.md#Process) of this project (at minimum one label for `T` required)
    * [ ] I have made corresponding changes to the documentation (if applicable)
    * [x] I have added tests that prove my fix is effective or that my feature works (if applicable)


    ## Bot Commands

    You can use the following bot commands in comments to help manage your PR:

    **Labeling (Self-service for contributors):**
    * `/cmd label T1-FRAME` - Add a single label
    * `/cmd label T1-FRAME R0-no-crate-publish-required` - Add multiple labels
    * `/cmd label T6-XCM D2-substantial I5-enhancement` - Add multiple labels at once
    * See [label documentation](https://paritytech.github.io/labels/doc_polkadot-sdk.html) for all available labels

    **Other useful commands:**
    * `/cmd fmt` - Format code (cargo +nightly fmt and taplo)
    * `/cmd prdoc` - Generate PR documentation
    * `/cmd bench` - Run benchmarks
    * `/cmd update-ui` - Update UI tests
    * `/cmd --help` - Show help for all available commands
crates:
- name: bridge-hub-rococo-runtime
  bump: major
- name: bridge-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: bridge-hub-test-utils
  bump: major
